{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1788267973,"nonce":"0M1FjqPtDeV9DxUzGuJNvkcMlD8=","target":"8b4839fe590ce65c7a3cb4fcae1e33c68c75a879ec7bbefe8aa5bffb6e9d1738","message":"Small, session 13, bench `20260901T121508`. Fix in `DevVerbs.cs` + `Blockers.cs`; lands before `c718e4a` and is consumed by it.\n\n\n`dev:spawn-thing {def:\"HiTechResearchBench\", pos:[125,128], mode:\"direct\"}` refused with `reason: \"Interaction spot is blocked by granite.\"` and `blocker: {def:\"WoodLog\", label:\"wood\", at:[125,128], removal:\"none\"}` (`results/accs13-026-devspawnthing.json`, journal seq 38). The sentence names granite on the interaction cell (`[125,127]`, one south of the centre — `interactionCellOffset (0,0,-1)`); the blocker names a wood log on the target cell, with `removal:\"none\"` — the exact opposite of the truth (the granite is `mine`). `accs13-029` at `[124,129]` is the same defect with the target cell empty, so `blocker` degrades to a bare `Cell()` with no def at all.\n\n\n`DevVerbs.WhyNoSpawn` returns a string. It knows which branch refused and, for the interaction branch, only the `AcceptanceReport.Reason` from `GenConstruct.InteractionCellStandable` — which names the thing's label but not its cell. The caller then does `Blockers.At(map, target, why)`, and `Blockers.At` is documented as \"the obstacle AT A CELL\" — it faithfully describes the target cell, which is not the cell that refused. Session-13 finding A fixed the null-blocker half of this (`GetFirstBuilding` → `Blockers.At`) and left the which-cell half.\n\n\n`WhyNoSpawn` returns a struct `{reason, cell, thing, tier}` — `tier` ∈ `footprint | interaction | terrain | bounds` — rather than a string. For the interaction branch it re-walks `ThingUtility.InteractionCellsWhenAt(def, c, rot, map)` and applies `InteractionCellStandable`'s own predicate (`passability != Standable || def == thingDef`, then `entityDefToBuild`) to find the cell and the thing; for the wipe-scan branch the thing is the one it already found; for terrain the cell is the first failing `OccupiedRect` cell (walk the rect the way `CanBuildOnTerrain` does, not the centre). `Blockers.At` is called with THAT cell, and the failure row gains `cell_role` (= tier) so a reader knows the blocker is off-footprint without arithmetic. The `Near`-mode branch (`branch ?? why`) gets the same struct.\n\n\n- Replay: bench with rock one cell south of the centre. `failed[0].blocker` is `{def:\"Granite\", at:[125,127], removal:\"mine\"}` and `failed[0].cell_role == \"interaction\"`; the target cell's wood log appears nowhere in the row.\n- A target cell that is itself rock: `cell_role == \"footprint\"`, blocker at the target, as today.\n- Unbuildable terrain in a non-centre footprint cell: blocker `at` is that cell, not the centre.\n- `accept/s13-mod-surface.py` phase 1 shapes still pass; add `1.5x`/`1.6x` checks asserting `blocker.at != at` for the interaction case (the shape rule: assert the key exists, never `eq(None)`).","files":null}]}